DIFFERENCES MCV & LARAVEL
MVC is an architectural pattern. Laravel is a PHP framework that implements MVC (and much more).
- MVC = Blueprint (the design)
- Laravel = House (built using that blueprint)


WHAT ARE WE GOING TO BUILD?
We are going to build fully functional MVC Framework using PHP 7.4 which can be installed and used using composer.

SEVERAL FEATURES OF THE FRAMEWORK
- Custom Routing                    - Validations
- Composer                          - Registration/Login
- Controllers                       - Simple Active Record
- Views/Layouts                     - Session Flash messages
- Models                            - Middlewares
- Migrations                        - Application events
- Form widget classes               - Framework reusable/installable core
- Processing of request data

