LEARNING INFO: 
-----------------------------------
    To install composer to project
        > composer init

    Add autoload dependencies at composer.json
        "autoload": {
            "psr-4": {
                "App\\": "./"
            }
        },
    
    Then, update the composer 
        > composer update

    Then can using above class label and call class
        namespace App\core; -- label
        use App\core\Router; -- call
-----------------------------------
VITUAL HOSTS: XAMMP
-----------------------------------
    Make Vitual Host server (changing "localhost/mvc_framework/public/" to "mvc-framework.test") -- for not give user have access to composer.json

    1. Open File /Applications/XAMPP/etc/extra/httpd-vhosts.conf tambah Virtual Host server

    <VirtualHost *:80>
        DocumentRoot "/Applications/XAMPP/htdocs"
        ServerName localhost

        <Directory "/Applications/XAMPP/htdocs">
            AllowOverride All
            Require all granted
        </Directory>
    </VirtualHost>


    <VirtualHost *:80>
        DocumentRoot "/Applications/XAMPP/htdocs/mvc_framework/public"
        ServerName mvc-framework.test

        <Directory "/Applications/XAMPP/htdocs/mvc_framework/public">
            AllowOverride All
            Require all granted
        </Directory>
    </VirtualHost>

    2. Enable Virtual Host - /Applications/XAMPP/etc/httpd.conf
    - remove # to uncomment
    Include etc/extra/httpd-vhosts.conf

    3. Open Terminal + add 127.0.0.1 servername
    > sudo nano /etc/hosts
    ##
    # Host Database
    #
    ##
    127.0.0.1       localhost
    255.255.255.255 broadcasthost
    ::1             localhost
    127.0.0.1       mvc-framework.test

    > Control + O (save)
    > Enter
    > Control + X (exit)

    4. Safari problem must have "http://" at URL like this (http://mvc-framework.test/contact),  if not it will open google.
