-----------------------------------
MIGRATIONS FOLDER + FILE    
-----------------------------------
Migrations is a file which contain the changes of the database. 

In general are commited and push, so when ever someone else pull you repository and run some specify script it should apply migration to your local database.
- We give the name for migrations class m0001_...php because class name cannot start with number and we can add another class like "m0002_something.php".

ENV FILE

 Using .env file must import this dependency inside composer
 > composer require vlucas/phpdotenv
 Then can using this command inside index.php and migrations.php
    $dotenv = Dotenv\Dotenv::createImmutable(__DIR__);
    $dotenv->load();
 Using it to database.php with PDO connection.

-----------------------------------
DBMODEL file (ORM - OBJECT-RELATIONAL MAPPING)
-----------------------------------
This will be a model which be a mapping, it to much like ORM models (object-relational mapping) 
and it will map user model/classes into database tables.
-----------------------------------
DIFFERENCES DBMODEL, MODEL AND USERMODEL
-----------------------------------
Soalan ini sangat bagus sebab ini menyentuh design pattern MVC + Active Record. 
Kenapa LoginForm extend Model, tetapi User extend DbModel?

Jawapan ringkas:
 - Model → untuk model yang hanya pegang data + validation + form logic (tidak terus berhubung dengan database).
 - DbModel → untuk model yang mewakili database table dan perlu operasi (CRUD, query, table mapping).
 - UserModel → Authentication & identity (login, current user, display  name, primary key untuk sesi, dll.)
 - User → Implementasi sebenar model pengguna (users table)

 https://chatgpt.com/s/t_6a6c0a47e0988191a59fba24e3f0d23f

 Model (abstract)
   ▲
DbModel (abstract)
   ▲
UserModel (abstract)
   ▲
  User

-----------------------------------
CONCEPT FOR THIS MVC
-----------------------------------
Soalan ini bagus sebab ini adalah bahagian paling penting dalam 
MVC framework: bagaimana data dari index.php boleh sampai ke 
AuthController::register(Request $request).

Jawapan pendek: 
    index.php tidak pass $request secara terus.Yang create dan pass 
    Request object ialah Router, kemudian Router panggil Controller method.

                Browser
                    |
                    | GET /register
                    |
                    v
                public/index.php
                    |
                    v
                $app->run()
                    |
                    v
                Application
                    |
                    v
                Router->resolve()
                    |
                    v
                new Request() + new Response() 
                    |
                    v
        AuthController->register($request)

*NOTES: We should never uses any class inside the core, with is outside the core 
        because idea of the core it that same every installation and the rest of the file can be changes.
-----------------------------------
CLASS REFERENCE DYNAMIC
-----------------------------------
Soalan ini berkaitan dengan PHP class reference. User::class bukan memanggil file User.php, 
tetapi mengambil nama penuh class (fully qualified class name) sebagai string.

Dalam User.php: 
    namespace App\models;

    class User extends DbModel
    {

    }

Bila anda tulis:
    User::class
PHP akan tukarkan kepada:
    "App\models\User"

Example: Dlm index.php
    $config = [
        'userClass' => \App\models\User::class, -- Use on this
        'db' => [
            'dsn' => $_ENV['DB_DSN'],
            'user' => $_ENV['DB_USER'],
            'password' => $_ENV['DB_PASSWORD'],
        ]
    ];

So bila guna 'userClass': (Contoh dalam constructor Application.php)
    $this->userClass::primaryKey();
PHP baca: 
    $className = "App\models\User";
    $className::primaryKey();
sama mcm: 
    App\models\User::primaryKey(); 

IMPORTANCE: dengan syarat primaryKey() static function, tidak kena buat Object untuk access.

*NOTED: class reference and object instance 2 benda berbeza.
