SUBTOPIC: MAKE CORE INSTALLABLE COMPOSER PACKAGE
-----------------------------------
This will make the core folder be packagist like autoload, you need install it and delete the original core.

We want only Core folder will be publish. So, run this all command after > cd core.

STEP 1: Create repository inside Git Hub and push by this command.
STEP 2: Create package acc and submit package.

REPOSITORY GITHUB
    Create name repo PHP-MCV-Core
COMMAND TO PUSH:
    git init : Initializes a brand new, empty Git tracking system in your local folder.
    git status :  Shows which files have been modified, deleted, or are currently untracked.
    git add . : Stages all of your new and modified files, preparing them to be saved.
    git status
    git commit -m "your message" : Permanently saves your staged changes into your local version history.
    git branch -M main : Renames your default local branch to "main" (the standard naming convention on GitHub).    
    git remote add origin git@github.com:nabilzafarin/PHP-MCV-Core.git : Connects your local folder to a newly created, empty remote repository on GitHub.
    git push -u origin main : Uploads your local saved code up to your online GitHub repository for the first time.

CREATE ACCOUNT ADD PACKAGIST.ORG
    https://packagist.org - username: NabilShah pass:nabilP1P4

SUBMIT PACKAGE
    nabilshah@GulaHack-MacBook-Air core % composer init
    Package name (<vendor>/<name>) [nabilshah/core]: ns/php-mvc-core
    
    Then, click all yes it will create composer.json and .gitignore inside core folder.

PUSH COMPOSER.JSON AND .GITIGNORE FILE
    git init
    git status
    git add .
    git commit -m "Create composer.json and .gitignore"
    git push -u origin main

CREATE TAG inside GitHub
    Create New Release 
    Tag: Press Select Tag and Create new tag (v1.0.0)
    Title: Inital release

COPY LINK TO SUMBIT PACKAGE
    
    - Copy this link https://github.com/nabilzafarin/PHP-MCV-Core
    - Paste on Packagist.org at page Submit Package on Repository URL (Git/Svn/Hg)
    - It will check vendor name inside composer.json "name": "ns/php-mvc-core", ns already Used. Change to another vendor name "name": "gulahack/php-mvc-core". 
    - Push back Composer.json file into github

THE PACKAGE AT ANOTHER PROJECT

Must changing the namespace inside all folder
    App\core -> App\core

by refering the autoload inside composer.json at core, if don't have at it inside composer.json
        "autoload": {
                "psr-4": {
                    "gulahack\\PhpMvcCore\\": "src/"
                }
            },

    - Then push to github and make a new release v1.0.2 with title "change namespace" so the packagist will pick up the latest version.
    - Click update button at your page packagist : https://packagist.org/packages/gulahack/php-mvc-core

Also add "license": "MIT", inside the composer.json at core
    {
        "name": "gulahack/php-mvc-core",
        "license": "MIT",
        "authors": [
            {
                "name": "GulaHack",
                "email": "muhdnabilshah@gmail.com"
            }
        ],
        "autoload": {
            "psr-4": {
                "gulahack\\PhpMvcCore\\": "src/"
            }
        },
        "require": {}
    }

    - Then push to github and make a new release v1.0.3 with title "add license mit" so the packagist will pick up the latest version.
    - Click update button at your page packagist : https://packagist.org/packages/gulahack/php-mvc-core
    - Try run at command: composer require gulahack/php-mvc-core:dev-master or composer require gulahack/php-mvc-core:^v1.0.3
    - Check the vendor folder it will see the gulahack/php-mvc-core folders that contain core inside it.
    - if don't have .git file just command : composer require gulahack/php-mvc-core:^v1.0.3 --prefer-source

    - To remove back composer remove gulahack/php-mvc-core

